  "lesson": "## Why this first\n\n\n  Every song in C major is built from these seven notes. The scale is the alphabet; chords and melodies are the words. Play with your right hand starting on middle C (the C nearest the middle of the keyboard).\n\n\n  Fingering going up: thumb 1, 2, 3, then tuck the thumb under to 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. Coming down is the mirror: 5 4 3 2 1, then cross the 3rd finger over the thumb, 3 2 1. The thumb tuck is the whole skill here; go slow enough that it never feels rushed.\n\n\n  Listen for the pattern of gaps: two whole steps, a half step, three whole steps, a half step. That W W H W W W H recipe is what makes anything sound \"major\".\n",
